From: RenoDX AMD bridge experiment
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] dlss: validate AMD support before slSetD3DDevice

Some Streamline titles query DLSS support before they call slSetD3DDevice. Waiting
for the live game device makes those titles hide or reject DLSS too early.

Use the exact DXGI adapter LUID supplied by sl::AdapterInfo. The helper creates a
short-lived D3D12 device on that adapter and asks the signed FidelityFX loader for
available upscaler providers with ffxQueryDescGetVersions. Only return support
when that provider query succeeds; do not spoof every AMD adapter blindly.

slIsFeatureLoaded intentionally remains live-device/backend-gated. Streamline's
own API contract requires a DX/VK device before that function is called.

--- a/src/utils/dlss/streamline_v2.hpp
+++ b/src/utils/dlss/streamline_v2.hpp
@@
 #include "./amd_bridge.hpp"
 #include "./ffx_upscale_backend_dx12.hpp"
+#include "./ffx_support_probe_dx12.hpp"
 #include "./DXGIFactoryWrapper.hpp"
@@
 static decltype(&slIsFeatureSupported) Real_slIsFeatureSupported = nullptr;
 static sl::Result Hooked_slIsFeatureSupported(sl::Feature feature, const sl::AdapterInfo& adapterInfo) {
-  if (feature == sl::kFeatureDLSS
-      && renodx::utils::dlss::amd_bridge::IsBackendAvailable()) {
-    return sl::Result::eOk;
+  if (feature == sl::kFeatureDLSS) {
+    if (renodx::utils::dlss::amd_bridge::IsBackendAvailable()
+        || renodx::utils::dlss::amd_bridge::ffx_dx12::ProbeAdapterSupport(adapterInfo)) {
+      return sl::Result::eOk;
+    }
   }
   return Real_slIsFeatureSupported(feature, adapterInfo);
 }

